<p:sld xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:p="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/presentationml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships"><p:cSld><p:spTree><p:nvGrpSpPr><p:cNvPr id="1" name=""/><p:cNvGrpSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvGrpSpPr><p:grpSpPr/><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="2" name="TextBox 1"/><p:cNvSpPr txBox="1"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="365760" y="384048"/><a:ext cx="11430000" cy="822960"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr wrap="square"><a:spAutoFit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:r><a:rPr sz="3200" b="1"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="D2AE6C"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Urbanist"/></a:rPr><a:t>CONCLUSION</a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="3" name="TextBox 2"/><p:cNvSpPr txBox="1"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="548640" y="1554480"/><a:ext cx="11064240" cy="4389120"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr wrap="square"><a:spAutoFit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr algn="l"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="115000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="2000"/></a:spcAft></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr sz="1900" b="1"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="0C5394"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Urbanist"/></a:rPr><a:t>Synthetic Silence turns "is this AI response trustworthy" from a tone judgment into a measurable, per-claim signal</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr sz="1900" b="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="0C5394"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Urbanist"/></a:rPr><a:t> -- an information void score built from real evidence retrieval, not from the model's own confidence.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr algn="l"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="115000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="2000"/></a:spcAft></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr sz="1500" b="1"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="D2AE6C"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Urbanist"/></a:rPr><a:t>It is shipped as a working system</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr sz="1500" b="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="0C5394"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Urbanist"/></a:rPr><a:t>: a FastAPI backend with auth, a 5-signal risk-scoring engine, a research dashboard (Live Analysis, History, Analytics, Void Map, Compare, Settings), and a Chrome extension -- all backed by 115 passing automated tests.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr algn="l"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="115000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="2000"/></a:spcAft></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr sz="1500" b="1"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="D2AE6C"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Urbanist"/></a:rPr><a:t>It is honestly evaluated</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr sz="1500" b="0"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="0C5394"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Urbanist"/></a:rPr><a:t>: five real live test cases surfaced both what works (evidence-rich domains correctly clear true claims) and what does not yet (sparse or non-academic evidence produces false positives and false negatives) -- disclosed, not hidden.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr algn="l"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="115000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="800"/></a:spcAft></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr sz="1350" b="0" i="1"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="94A3B8"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Urbanist"/></a:rPr><a:t>The original TT-WGAN-GP research direction was retired on its own mathematical merits</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr sz="1350" b="0" i="1"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="94A3B8"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Urbanist"/></a:rPr><a:t> (see paper.tex); this system is what replaced it -- a retrieval-and-heuristics pipeline that is smaller in ambition but actually runs, is actually tested, and says exactly what it does and does not know.</a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp></p:spTree></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr></p:sld>